From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:32:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: a damage hit during a camera stall still rumbles, and
 only a save load is skipped; built, untested on console

The large-damage path tested GameState::IsInGame() at the hit, which is false whenever the camera has not updated for five frames; a Guardian beam or a long fall that landed in a streaming hitch was logged as the load call and played nothing. The first in-game frame is latched now (IsInGame() true once), so the load call at 0x02CAB32C is still skipped and every later hit plays, camera fresh or not.
---
 src/game/botw/player/player.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/game/botw/player/player.cpp b/src/game/botw/player/player.cpp
index a5152eb..f99e3bb 100644
--- a/src/game/botw/player/player.cpp
+++ b/src/game/botw/player/player.cpp
@@ -144,8 +144,13 @@ static void PlayDamageRumble(uint32_t stateNamePtr, const char* path) {
     };
 
     // 0x02CAB32C also runs once while a save loads, before the first in-game frame: that is not a hit and the motor
-    // must not buzz at boot; the line says which call this was.
-    if (largeDamage && !GameState::IsInGame()) {
+    // must not buzz at boot; the line says which call this was. The first in-game frame is latched, not IsInGame()'s
+    // answer now: that also asks the camera, which a streaming hitch leaves a few frames stale (patch bettervr 0006),
+    // and a hit that lands in the hitch is still a hit.
+    static bool s_seenFirstInGameFrame = false;
+    if (!s_seenFirstInGameFrame && GameState::IsInGame())
+        s_seenFirstInGameFrame = true;
+    if (largeDamage && !s_seenFirstInGameFrame) {
         say("none, before the first in-game frame (load)");
         return;
     }
